Student Performance Prediction Using Machine Learning

Project Title

Student Performance Prediction Using Machine Learning



Abstract

Student Performance Prediction Using Machine Learning is a data-driven system designed to analyze student-related factors and predict academic performance. The system uses machine learning algorithms to identify patterns in attendance, study hours, previous academic records, assignments, and other educational factors. The prediction helps teachers and institutions identify students who may require additional support and enables early intervention to improve academic outcomes.



Problem Statement

Educational institutions often face challenges in identifying students who are at risk of poor academic performance. Traditional evaluation methods usually detect problems only after examinations are completed. There is a need for an intelligent system that can analyze student data and predict performance in advance, allowing educators to take proactive measures and improve student success rates.



Project Objectives


Collect and analyze student academic data.

Preprocess and clean the dataset for machine learning.

Build predictive models to estimate student performance.

Identify key factors affecting academic success.

Provide early warnings for students at academic risk.

Assist educators in making data-driven decisions.



